              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic ḥawāla, \"a handing over, custody\": the room where a person handed over to the police is held. It is not जेल, prison: हवालात (havālāt) is for a night or two."
            }
          ]
        },
